wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:3:tags: [offer, pricing, performance-fee, risk-reversal, pulse-system, contract]
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:11:The first commercial offer Pulsify sells. Built around [[concepts/pulse-system-mechanism|the Pulse System]]. Base fee plus performance share. Sold to coaches with a working offer and the will to execute. The headline guarantee is **$100,000 in new revenue within 90 days, or Pulsify works free until they hit it.**
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:13:> Risk-reversal under review: [[synthesis/offer-v2-risk-reversal]] proposes replacing the unbounded "$100k or free" headline with a credible, bounded, execution-gated structure that closes better in the trust recession and caps founder downside. Economics (base + performance) unchanged. Founder decision pending.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:21:Pulsify installs the full back-end of a coaching business — personal brand, content engine, funnel, sales infrastructure, and a custom AI agent that replaces a 3-person VA team — for a base fee plus a 25–30% performance share, and guarantees the client makes at least $100,000 in new revenue inside 90 days or we work free until they do.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:27:1. **Open at $5,000 base + 30% performance.** This is the default and the floor on the base.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:32:Both base AND performance fee are mandatory. There is no path that drops one. The base funds the build; the performance fee aligns Pulsify with growth. Skipping either breaks the model.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:36:**Payment terms — performance:** weekly settlement against attributable revenue (see definition below). Reported every Friday from the integrated payment-processor view.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:40:## Performance fee — attribution and mechanics
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:46:**Duration:** no ceiling, no time cap. The performance fee runs as long as the assets Pulsify built are running and the engagement is active. If the client wants to terminate the performance share, they terminate the engagement and Pulsify stops maintaining the system.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:56:**Continuation has no time cap and no hour cap.** Pulsify continues as long as it takes. The performance fee continues to apply on revenue collected during continuation.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-offer-v1.md:88:- **No offer at all** ("I just post about trading"). They need offer creation first. Scope a separate $5k engagement, no performance fee on that scope.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-delivery-sop.md:64:- Brand Brain populated inside the client's own Claude project. Knowledge base: voice samples, mechanism, offer details, past content performance, competitor set.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-delivery-sop.md:128:- **If hit:** celebrate, collect testimonial, schedule case-study production, propose continuation terms (renewal at full base + same performance share, or transition to performance-only at the founder's discretion).
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-delivery-sop.md:129:- **If missed:** continuation triggers per the offer page. No additional base. Performance fee continues. Engagement runs until target is hit. The week-12 call sets the new immediate-priority list and new weekly cadence.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-delivery-sop.md:148:- Final email: links, credentials returned, performance-fee final settlement schedule.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-dashboard-workstream.md:110:- Hook-pattern performance tracking.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-dashboard-workstream.md:116:- DMs/Looms sent (today, this week, 30-day, all-time).
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-dashboard-workstream.md:120:- Cash collected (base + performance fee accrual).
wiki\playbooks\format-invention-pipeline.md:64:Track per format: birth date, performance trend, and the 3-6 month review. At review: innovate (if working), retire (if decaying), or reinvent (pipeline from stage 2). The founder's calendar must actually contain the pipeline time — call-batching (2 call days, 3 thinking days) exists precisely to fund stages 1-3.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:11:The canonical service agreement Pulsify sends after a close. Templatized from the Nick Furr and Jacob Thomas agreements, rewritten to match the v1 offer (base fee + performance + $100k guarantee + Turkey payment rails + Pulse System scope). Send via DocuSign.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:30:| Performance share | 25% | 20% | 25% or 30% per branch |
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:93:**Performance Share:** The Operator shall receive {{PERFORMANCE_PERCENT}}% of all attributable revenue collected by the Client during the engagement, payable on a weekly settlement cadence within five (5) business days of the close of each calendar week.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:95:**Attribution Rule:** All revenue collected by the Client from the date the Operator is integrated into the Client's CRM and payment processor is attributable to the Operator, with the sole exception of leads that were already in active negotiation with a scheduled close date prior to integration. After integration, every revenue event collected counts toward the performance share because the Operator owns the systems generating, processing, and tracking them.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:103:## III. Engagement Term and Performance Guarantee
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:107:**Performance Guarantee:** The Operator guarantees that the Client shall collect at least USD 100,000 in new attributable revenue (as defined in Section II) within the 90-day Paid Term.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:109:**Continuation:** If the Client has not collected USD 100,000 in attributable revenue by the end of the Paid Term, the Operator shall continue to provide the Services at no additional Base Fee until the threshold is achieved. There is no time cap and no hour cap on the continuation period. The Performance Share continues to apply on all revenue collected during continuation.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:111:**Termination by Client:** The Client may terminate the engagement at any time with seven (7) days' written notice. Termination ends the Operator's obligation to deliver Services, ends the Operator's obligation to maintain installed systems, and ends the Performance Share on revenue collected after termination. Base Fee installments already due remain payable.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:120:- Performance Share payments are non-refundable, as they are directly tied to revenue already collected by the Client.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:148:Without integration, the Operator cannot perform the Services or compute the Performance Share. Failure to provide integration within fourteen (14) days of the Effective Date is grounds for termination under Section III.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:189:**BY SIGNING BELOW, EACH PARTY ACKNOWLEDGES THAT IT UNDERSTANDS AND AGREES TO ALL OF THE AFOREMENTIONED TERMS, INCLUDING THOSE RELATED TO SERVICE FEES, THE PERFORMANCE GUARANTEE, THE INTEGRATION REQUIREMENT, REFUND POLICY, AND CONFIDENTIALITY.**
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:208:| `{{PERFORMANCE_PERCENT}}` | Negotiated share per offer page | 25 or 30 |
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:224:- **Performance share on continuation past 12 months.** v1 has no cap. If a client crosses 12 months in continuation, the Operator is doing unbounded free work. Founder accepts this risk as of 2026-05-10 ([[playbooks/pulsify-offer-v1#open-questions--gaps]]). Revisit when the first stress event arrives.
wiki\playbooks\pulsify-contract-template-v1.md:232:- [[playbooks/pulsify-offer-v1]] — pricing tree, performance attribution, guarantee, integration requirement.
wiki\synthesis\offer-v2-risk-reversal.md:33:Three structures, in order of how I'd deploy them. They stack with the existing base + performance model and the negotiation tree in v1.
wiki\synthesis\offer-v2-risk-reversal.md:49:> "Worst case: month one is pure performance. Small base, we split new revenue 80/20 in your favor, and if you don't see [conservative number] you walk and I keep nothing. Best case we lock the 90-day engagement."
wiki\synthesis\offer-v2-risk-reversal.md:57:- Base + performance dual structure and the [[playbooks/pulsify-offer-v1]] negotiation tree ($5k+30% open, $5k+30% floor).
wiki\frameworks\call-funnel-framework.md:62:- **Frequency cap awareness** — once a prospect has seen an ad 3–5+ times, performance drops
wiki\synthesis\vsl-patterns\daniel-fazio-get-clients-challenge-analysis.md:46:- recent business performance numbers
wiki\synthesis\portal-content-studio-spec.md:11:Founder direction, verbatim intent: this is NOT the heavily coded funnels stack — it is a dashboard for clients, with a login and password, where a client checks their revenue, their content, the performance, the metrics, the team, how things are moving, their plans, and their to-do lists — and where the Instagram section is exactly where they generate their story sequences, carousels, and YouTube content. Grounded in both creator corpora and in everything Pulsify has already built. Build lane: Codex implements, Claude specs and reviews; fire gated on founder's morning go.
wiki\synthesis\portal-content-studio-spec.md:31:3. **Performance & metrics** — the measurement doctrine from both corpora (full inventory below). Week-over-week only, never month-vs-month (SooWei). Prescriptive, not just descriptive: every red metric links to the fix (the Action Engine principle from the dashboard product vision).
wiki\synthesis\portal-content-studio-spec.md:33:5. **Momentum ("how things are moving")** — the weekly recap block: shipped last week, shipping this week, deltas on the 3-5 headline numbers; monthly recap ritual notes (Niksetting's one-hour dashboard review, productized).
wiki\synthesis\portal-content-studio-spec.md:46:- **Completion %** (his launch benchmark: 71.9% over ~9 slides), **per-slide views**, **DMs + interactions per sequence**, **profile visits from stories**, **compared performance vs prior sequences**, and a **copy log** so winning copy is reusable ("the system capitalizes on all the copy").
wiki\funnel-hacks\creators\iman-gadzhi\funnel-layer.md:52:5. **3 Core Pillars** — Experience / Information / Connections. "Information" pillar explicitly promises open books — campaign performance, event ROI, real metrics. Transparency as differentiator.
