wiki\synthesis\dashboards-audit-and-portal-strategy-2026-07-12.md:49:1. **Proof they're winning** (Revenue + Performance): real payments, follower growth, drop-off improving week over week, dollars-per-follower climbing. The client sees the system working in numbers, not vibes.
wiki\playbooks\content-operating-rhythm.md:34:The ratified anti-batch method (Amer case): create 2 pieces Monday (~45 min, not 8 hours) -> read the data Tuesday -> apply + create 2 more Wednesday -> repeat. Why not batch a month: staleness hides the growth signal, and "the only reason a customer buys is the moment they see someone grow" — a month-old batch can't carry this week's growth. Minimum: create every other day.
wiki\playbooks\content-operating-rhythm.md:56:1. **Client deliverable:** install the calendar in Week 1 — the posting cadence, the every-other-day loop, the call-batching restructure, the delegation map. The dashboard's Content and Momentum sections render it; the Performance section runs the weekly ritual.
wiki\playbooks\content-operating-rhythm.md:58:3. **The cadence is a health metric:** "sequences this week vs the 3-floor" is a P3 dashboard number; cadence collapse is the earliest churn-risk signal.
wiki\playbooks\client-scaling.md:75:Ceiling: organic scale is limited by reach. The ceiling is typically $30K–$50K/month for a solo operator without ads, depending on niche and content performance.
