wiki\synthesis\client-dashboard-redesign-spec-2026-07-12.md:11:The founder-approved redesign of the client dashboard, designed with the impeccable craft flow (product register, Trakyo visual contract) and handed to Codex to build to production quality against the live data. The Studio is the centerpiece. Design north-star: the live preview at `pulsify-funnels.pages.dev/portal-preview/` (source: `output/standard-preview/portal-preview/index.html`) — treat it as the composition/hierarchy/interaction contract, not a screenshot to trace.
wiki\synthesis\client-dashboard-redesign-spec-2026-07-12.md:15:- **Design language:** Trakyo. Tokens in `output/standard-preview/shared/pulsify-ui.css` (money-green `#0ea968` + `#34d399`, Inter UI, JetBrains Mono tabular numbers, 3-tier soft shadows, 16px radius, light/dark). The preview file uses the same system inline — reconcile into the shared stylesheet.
wiki\synthesis\client-dashboard-redesign-spec-2026-07-12.md:64:- **Home / "This week"** — replaces Momentum. A money hero (cash this week + all-time + sparkline), followers, $/follower, DMs, a **"Your next move"** prescription card (the diagnosis engine surfaced on the overview, one action into Studio), and shipped-this-week / owed-this-week lists. The one-screen login view.
wiki\synthesis\client-dashboard-redesign-spec-2026-07-12.md:69:- **Performance** — KPI cards + a **slide-by-slide retention curve** (SVG area chart, the cliff marked) + a **type leaderboard** (completion bars, top-to-bottom) + sequence rows with bar strips (drop slide in rose) + a "Log sequence" modal (feed the engine) + a reach donut. This is the live P3 data plus the tracking depth the founder asked for.
wiki\synthesis\client-dashboard-redesign-spec-2026-07-12.md:86:- This is a real feature build (new data surfaces), not a pure reskin. Structure it in passes: shell + shared tokens -> Studio (the centerpiece) -> Revenue settings/integrations -> Team -> Home/Performance/Plans/To-dos -> states + responsive + a11y.
wiki\synthesis\client-acquisition-renovation-2026-07-03.md:20:- **Client portal:** stop being a data viewer, become the weekly proof that the $10K engagement is working — every screen answers "what did Pulsify move for me this week."
wiki\synthesis\client-acquisition-renovation-2026-07-03.md:69:- A small scoreboard strip on top (sends today/this week, replies, calls booked, cash collected) — the only place aggregate numbers appear on this screen.
wiki\synthesis\client-acquisition-renovation-2026-07-03.md:106:The Client OS shell is competent but it is a data viewer: tabs of funnel rows, content items, call notes. A client paying $5–12K doesn't want to browse tables; they want to know the engagement is working, what happened this week, and what's next. The portal is also the sales asset shown to prospects mid-close, so it has to look like the $10K product.
