wiki\content-engine\pulsify-vsl-v1.md:113:I mean: AI compresses the build time on every piece of this from weeks to days. A content system that took a team six weeks—AI runs it in a week. An onboarding automation, a contract sequence, a lead qualification flow—built and live this week, not next month.
wiki\content-engine\pulsify-vsl-v1.md:171:The sales infrastructure: a setter and a closer, hired, trained, scripted, tracked. Paid on performance. They eat when you eat.
wiki\content-engine\packaging-rules.md:15:Pulsify's clients spend time and resources producing content. Packaging failure wastes that production entirely — the video gets made, posted, and ignored. Packaging rules are the set of constraints that Pulsify applies before any video is titled or thumbnailed, so that production effort is spent on ideas that have a documented path to performance.
wiki\content-engine\packaging-rules.md:131:- The "complete vs. repeat title" distinction from Ayman is not fully explored. A worked comparison with performance data would sharpen this rule considerably.
wiki\concepts\profile-funnel.md:83:- Pulsify-verified performance data: none yet; first deployment is the calibration run.
wiki\content-engine\reel-capture-to-content-engine.md:58:Every reel that posts is logged into the same drop-off and performance diagnosis the story sequences use. After a few weeks the engine can say which angles and which kinds of thoughts actually convert for this creator, so the intuition stops being a guess. This directly answers the founder's stated hesitation: you start on validated angles, and the system builds the data that proves which of your thoughts are worth more.
