claude-memory\project_dashboard_v3_backlog.md:34:**TRAKYO DESIGN DIRECTION (2026-06-25, user asleep/autonomous mandate):** User wants a Trakyo.io-grade redesign — "go crazy, multiple paths, not dogshit basic." Trakyo = "Track Every Dollar From YouTube": revenue attribution tying every click/opt-in/booking/sale to the exact YouTube video, via YouTube+Stripe+Calendly+Typeform; core view = per-content card (Cash Collected / Bookings / Form Submissions / Tracking Link Clicks + tabbed Performance-Over-Time chart + Recent Leads). This IS Pulsify's model → applies perfectly. I built a standalone premium prototype (NOT touching live): `pulsify-trakyo.html` (worktree) + Desktop `pulsify-trakyo-DIRECTION.html` + sent to user. Design = dark collapsible rail + light content (Linear/Vercel vibe), Inter, soft-shadow cards, emerald(money)/indigo accents, real SVG charts w/ sensible demo data, dark-mode toggle. Sections: Overview (KPIs + tabbed attribution chart + top content + leads), Content (rows → click opens attribution DRAWER = the Trakyo core), Clients (All/Nick/Jacob switcher in topbar + Total bar + per-offer revenue), Payments, Calendar, Integrations (11 connect cards: YouTube/Stripe/Calendly/Typeform/Kit/Fanbasis/Whop/Teachable/Tally/WebinarJam/ClickFunnels + manual-data-feed panel). Verified working, 0 errors. NEXT: on user approval, port this direction to the live dashboard + wire real data/integrations + fold in the rest of the backlog above. Tech stack to integrate natively: Typeform, Calendly, Kit, Stripe, Fanbasis, Whop, Teachable, Tally, WebinarJam, ClickFunnels, YouTube. Also wants Instagram as a dynamic page (reels covers shadowed + hover), cinematic Overview animation, expandable sidebar (done in proto), connectable manual data feed (done in proto).
claude-memory\project_dashboard_v3_backlog.md:36:**MERGE STARTED (2026-06-27, user approved "start the merge"):** Decided architecture = RESKIN IN PLACE, not rebuild — keep all 8.5k lines of live JS + real data (ytLeadsData 436 leads, CRM/Lead Studio, payouts/cashflow/payments/content-pipeline/health), graft the Trakyo design system on top + add Trakyo's net-new features. Working on a COPY: `awesome-bassi-d88340/index-trakyo.html`. **SHIPPED TO LIVE 2026-06-27** (user: "keep going and push it to live") — commit 09366bc FF on origin/main; live index.html is now Trakyo, Mirage backed up as index-mirage.html. Continued dev still happens on index-trakyo.html → redeploy per [[project_deploy_pipeline]]. Mechanism = registered Trakyo as a 10th THEME (`theme-trakyo`, set as this build's default) so it overrides cleanly; appended a "TRAKYO LAYER" CSS block before the first </style> (~line 3477). PHASE 1 DONE + VERIFIED via preview_eval (server `dashboard` in launch.json serves the worktree on :8765, load /index-trakyo.html): light palette (#f5f6f8 bg, emerald #0ea968 accent), Inter font, dark rail (#0b0d12) independent of palette, white soft-shadow cards, KPI .large tamed to 27px (backlog #9), active-nav emerald left-bar + killed the old emerald glow; all 11 tabs switch fine, real data intact. NEXT PHASES: (2) net-new Trakyo features — Content attribution DRAWER, Integrations page, client switcher — wired to real data; (3) fold in v3 backlog (calendar split, daily/monthly/quarterly revenue, multi-client navigator, bigger payouts pie, editable payments). Then user reviews → swap index-trakyo.html → index.html → deploy per [[project_deploy_pipeline]].
claude-memory\project_dashboard_v3_backlog.md:38:**PHASE 1.5 FIXES (2026-06-27, from live review):** (a) PAYMENTS ugly colors — root cause = ~50 HARDCODED Mirage hexes in JS/markup that ignore the theme system (this is WHY backlog #5 "all 9 themes faulty"). Fixed the two payments offenders: `chartColors` (~line 5428) and `typeColors` (~line 5716) → emerald #0ea968 / indigo #5b6cff / amber #f59e0b. STILL hardcoded elsewhere: STAGE_ACCENTS, CRM status/avatar colors (lines ~5388/7389/7516/8420). PROPOSED NEXT: full color-system sweep routing all hexes through CSS vars. (b) KPI values were Clash-Display 30px overflowing cards (the file has 3 separate <style> blocks; trakyo layer is in block 1 so later blocks override unless !important) → forced .kpi .v.large to JetBrains Mono 24px !important + clamp overflow. (c) CRM LAG (user's PC choked): default kanban board mounted ALL ~430 lead cards (gradient avatars + thumbnails + drag listeners), re-rendered on every keystroke. Fixed with pagination (upgraded 2026-06-27 from "Show more" to numbered PAGES per user ask): `crmPage` (0-idx) + `CRM_PAGE=60`/page; renderCrm slices `rows.slice(start,start+60)`; renderCrmPager() builds Prev/numbered-chips-with-ellipsis/Next + "x–y of N" into #crmMore (.crm-pager CSS); renderCrmBoard(shown, allRows) shows TRUE totals in col headers; renderCrmTable(shown, offset) numbers rows from page offset; search debounced 180ms; filters reset to page 1; page click scrolls list to top. Only one page mounts. SHIPPED LIVE commit 634c65f. Verified: page1=60 cards "1–60 of 430", page8=10 cards "421–430".
claude-memory\project_dashboard_v3_backlog.md:40:**VERIFY GOTCHA:** the preview server (python http.server on :8765 via session launch.json) + browser CACHE index-trakyo.html hard — after editing, reload with `location.href='/index-trakyo.html?v='+Date.now()` or assertions show STALE DOM. CRM tab + Payments tab both TIME OUT preview_screenshot (heavy DOM/chart anim) even at 60 cards — verify those via preview_eval assertions, screenshot only Overview/Metrics (and restart the preview server if the renderer wedges). [[project_dashboard_verification]] UPDATE: in a long session the screenshot renderer wedges on EVERY tab (even Overview) — don't over-rely on it; assertions + console-error check are the trustworthy verification.
claude-memory\project_dashboard_v3_backlog.md:42:**PHASE "DO EVERYTHING" (2026-06-27, user: do all flagged items, no phases) — ALL DONE + VERIFIED:** (1) COLOR-SYSTEM SWEEP — converted the JS color maps from hardcoded Mirage candy hexes to theme var() refs so they theme correctly in ALL 9 themes (fixes backlog #5 root cause): STAGE_ACCENTS, statusColor map (new/queued/researching/asset-built/contacted/replied/won/dead), avatar gradients avGrad (tier/source). Verified: CRM avatars + status now resolve to var(--blue) indigo etc., zero magenta/cyan/yellow literals left in rendered CRM. NOTE: in Trakyo --blue and --violet are both #5b6cff so some 2-stop gradients look flat (cosmetic, can differentiate later). (2) WHITE-ALPHA CHART LINES (invisible on light) — donut tracks/gridlines/bar-tracks/baselines `rgba(255,255,255,0.0x)` → `rgba(148,163,184,0.2x)` (works light+dark). (3) GRADIENT WASHES flattened on .feature-card/.hero-band/.ov-brief/.plan-vector under trakyo. (4) SERIF QUOTES (.hb-quote/.hh-quote/.plan-vector .quote) → Inter, font-style normal. (5) CALENDAR SPLIT (backlog #1 DONE) — moved booked-calls calendar + Next-up + booking-routing OUT of #tab-cashflow into NEW #tab-calendar with its own nav button (12 tabs now); relabeled cashflow nav "Cash flow"; globalized the `.cf-*` CSS (was `#tab-cashflow .cf` → `.cf`, 99 rules) so both tabs style correctly. Tab-switch just toggles .active (renders run once at init, target by ID) so no JS rewiring needed. Verified: calendar tab activates, 30-day grid renders there, cashflow no longer has it, 0 console errors. STILL OUTSTANDING from v3 backlog: daily/monthly/quarterly revenue views (#3), multi-client navigator (#6), editable payments (#7), Plan redesign (#10), client-portal payout calc (#11) + Phase 2 Trakyo net-new (attribution drawer, integrations page, client switcher). DONE since: bigger payouts pie (#4, shipped 5e91a3d).
claude-memory\project_dashboard_v3_backlog.md:44:**PORT TO CLIENT DASHBOARD (user note 2026-06-27):** part of this Trakyo operator work also needs to land on the CLIENT-facing dashboard = `client.html` (Atelier warm-cognac design, in stale worktree `wonderful-curran-8c48be/client.html`; copies on Desktop `pulsify-client-portal.html`/`pulsify-portal.html`; NOT yet integrated into awesome-bassi or deployed — see [[project_portal_reskin]]). Don't assume which pieces carry over — SCOPE it when we get there. Strong candidates: the attribution "track every dollar from YouTube" view (a client wants to see which of THEIR content drove revenue/bookings — arguably the #1 thing to give them), the payout calculator (already backlog #11), list pagination pattern, and the color-system-as-theme-vars approach. The client portal keeps its OWN Atelier look, so this is about porting FEATURES/patterns, not the Trakyo skin. Ties to [[project_dashboard_product_vision]] (productized $10K system → clients must see their gaps [[project_hta_dashboard]]).
